  "id": "DrugBank_DB00966 - MONDO_grouped_1200_1134_15512_5080_100078",
  "verbalization": "Telmisartan is implicated in the pathogenesis of hypertension through its interactions with multiple indications that ultimately converge on the disease. The evidence suggests that Telmisartan may be associated with Hypertension via indirect pathways, as it is linked to Hypertensive Disorder in two distinct paths. In Path 1, Telmisartan is associated with Cerebral Infarction, which in turn is linked to Ramipril, a drug used to treat hypertension. In Path 2 and 3, Telmisartan is directly linked to Hypertensive Disorder, which is then associated with Azelnidipine and Rilmenidine, both of which are used to manage hypertension. The final_score values indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, suggesting that Telmisartan may exert a role in the development or maintenance of hypertension through its effects on the cardiovascular system. The mechanisms underlying this relationship are likely mediated through the modulation of vascular tone and blood pressure regulation, though the exact pathways remain to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Telmisartan and hypertension, though further research is needed to confirm the precise role of Telmisartan in this context.",
